---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import { Code } from "astro:components";

// Composition preview: the global layers applied to realistic content, as
// opposed to /design, which is the reference. The post uses the real
// `.prose` styles from src/styles/prose.css; only the demo scaffolding and
// not-yet-extracted landing/UI samples are styled here.

const tsSample = `// Pin opsz to the body size: same bytes.
import { defineConfig, fontProviders } from "astro/config";

const BODY_OPSZ = 16;

export default defineConfig({
  fonts: [
    {
      provider: fontProviders.google(),
      name: "Newsreader",
      weights: ["200 800"],
      options: {
        experimental: { variableAxis: { opsz: [String(BODY_OPSZ)] } },
      },
    },
  ],
});

function payloadKB(bytes: number, precise = false) {
  return (bytes / 1024).toFixed(precise ? 2 : 1) + " KB";
}`;

const cssSample = `/* Code follows the palette, not a fixed theme */
:root {
  --astro-code-token-keyword: var(--accent);
  --astro-code-token-string: var(--secondary);
}

.prose pre {
  padding: var(--space-3);
  border-radius: 2px;
}`;
---

<Base title="Preview — whoami">
	<meta slot="head" name="robots" content="noindex" />
	<main class="page">

		<div class="switcher">
			<span class="chrome-label">Theme</span>
			<button class="thm" type="button" data-theme-set="light">Light</button>
			<button class="thm" type="button" data-theme-set="dark">Dark</button>
			<button class="thm" type="button" data-theme-set="system">System</button>
		</div>

		<p class="chrome-label">whoami — composition preview</p>
		<h1 class="page-title">Preview</h1>
		<p class="page-note">
			The tokens applied to realistic content, to judge whether the rules
			compose rather than whether the parts are correct. For the reference
			ladders, see <a href="/design">the style guide</a>. Switch themes above;
			every colour pairing on the page is contrast-verified.
		</p>

		<section class="frame">
			<p class="chrome-label">Long-form post</p>
			<article class="prose">
				<p class="meta">20 Sep 2026 · 8 min read · Typography</p>
				<h1>What a typeface costs when you measure it properly</h1>
				<p class="lead">
					I spent an afternoon assuming a font was expensive because it had
					too many axes, and discovered the expensive part was an axis I was
					not using at all.
				</p>

				<p>
					The site was loading 301 KB of fonts before a single word had been
					written. That number felt wrong, so I went looking for where it came
					from — and the answer turned out to contradict most of what I
					believed about variable fonts.
				</p>

				<h2>Ranges do not cost what you think</h2>
				<p>
					The intuition is that a wider axis range means a larger file, and
					that narrowing it saves bytes. It does not. Google Fonts serves one
					file per axis <em>combination</em>, and asking for a sub-range
					returns a byte-identical file to asking for the whole thing.
				</p>
				<pre><code>{`Newsreader italic 200..800   63.0 KB
Newsreader italic 400..600   63.0 KB   // identical
Newsreader italic 400        23.8 KB   // pinned`}</code></pre>
				<p>
					Only two operations change the payload: dropping an axis entirely,
					or pinning it to a single value. Everything else is decoration. Once
					that clicked, the optimisation became obvious — the
					<code>wdth</code> axis I had been carefully "narrowing" was costing 53
					KB and doing nothing, because nothing in the CSS ever set
					<code>font-stretch</code>.
				</p>

				<blockquote>
					<p>
						Buy the range only when one face is genuinely rendered across it.
						Otherwise pin it and take the optical correction for free.
					</p>
				</blockquote>

				<h3>The counter-intuitive part</h3>
				<p>
					Pinning <code>opsz</code> to the size you actually set text at is
					strictly better than omitting it. You get optical sizing tuned for
					your body copy at roughly zero cost over the default instance:
				</p>
				<ul>
					<li>Newsreader with <code>opsz</code> ranged 6–72: 128.8 KB</li>
					<li>Newsreader with <code>opsz</code> pinned at 16: 56.8 KB</li>
					<li>Newsreader with no <code>opsz</code> requested: 56.8 KB</li>
				</ul>
				<p>
					Same file size, better rendering. There is no trade-off to weigh —
					it is simply the correct thing to do, and I had been leaving it on
					the table.
				</p>

				<hr />
				<p class="footnote">
					All figures are the measured latin <code>woff2</code> payload, taken
					from the Google Fonts API rather than estimated. The full working is
					in the repository's design notes.
				</p>
			</article>
		</section>

		<section class="frame">
			<p class="chrome-label">Code blocks</p>
			<div class="code-samples">
				<div class="chrome-label" style="margin-bottom:var(--space-2)">TypeScript</div>
				<Code code={tsSample} lang="ts" theme="css-variables" />
				<div class="chrome-label" style="margin:var(--space-4) 0 var(--space-2)">CSS</div>
				<Code code={cssSample} lang="css" theme="css-variables" />
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="frame">
			<p class="chrome-label">Landing</p>
			<nav class="landing-nav">
				<span class="brand">Christian Gaetano</span>
				<a href="#">Writing</a>
				<a href="#">Work</a>
				<a href="#">Résumé</a>
				<a href="#">Colophon</a>
			</nav>
			<p class="hero">Engineer, occasional writer, persistent tinkerer.</p>
			<p class="hero-lead">
				I build things for the web and then take them apart to see why they
				worked. Currently rebuilding this site in public, one measured decision
				at a time.
			</p>
			<p class="chrome-label" style="margin-bottom:var(--space-2)">
				Selected work
			</p>
			<ul class="work-list">
				<li class="work-item">
					<h3>whoami</h3>
					<p>
						This site. Astro on Cloudflare Workers, with a type system built
						from measured font metrics rather than vibes.
					</p>
					<span class="year">2026</span>
				</li>
				<li class="work-item">
					<h3>Field notes</h3>
					<p>
						Short writing about the things that turn out to be more
						interesting than they first appear.
					</p>
					<span class="year">2026</span>
				</li>
				<li class="work-item">
					<h3>Earlier projects</h3>
					<p>
						A decade of work that predates this rebuild, gradually being
						migrated across.
					</p>
					<span class="year">2015–25</span>
				</li>
			</ul>
		</section>

		<section class="frame">
			<p class="chrome-label">Interface elements</p>
			<div class="ui-grid">
				<div class="ui-group">
					<h4>Buttons</h4>
					<div class="btn-row">
						<button class="btn solid" type="button">Read the post</button>
						<button class="btn" type="button">Subscribe</button>
						<button class="btn quiet" type="button">Cancel</button>
					</div>
				</div>

				<div class="ui-group">
					<h4>Tags</h4>
					<div class="tag-row">
						<span class="tag">Typography</span>
						<span class="tag">Astro</span>
						<span class="tag">Performance</span>
					</div>
				</div>

				<div class="ui-group">
					<h4>Form field</h4>
					<div class="field">
						<label for="preview-email">Email</label>
						<input
							id="preview-email"
							type="email"
							placeholder="you@example.com"
						/>
						<span class="hint">Used only for new posts. No more than monthly.</span>
					</div>
				</div>

				<div class="ui-group">
					<h4>Figures</h4>
					<span class="stat">169.7 KB</span>
					<span class="stat-label">total font payload</span>
				</div>

				<div class="ui-group">
					<h4>Inline link</h4>
					<p>
						A sentence with <a href="#">a link inside it</a> to check that the
						underline sits clear of Newsreader's descenders.
					</p>
				</div>

				<div class="ui-group">
					<h4>Metadata</h4>
					<p class="meta-sample">
						20 Sep 2026 · 8 min read · Typography
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>
	</main>

		<script>
			// Forces a theme by setting data-theme on <html>, which tokens.css maps
			// to color-scheme. "System" removes the attribute so the OS decides.
			const root = document.documentElement;
			const buttons = Array.from(document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>(".thm"));
			function apply(theme: string) {
				if (theme === "system") delete root.dataset.theme;
				else root.dataset.theme = theme;
				buttons.forEach((b) =>
					b.setAttribute("aria-pressed", String(b.dataset.themeSet === theme)),
				);
			}
			let theme = "system";
			try {
				theme = localStorage.getItem("whoami-theme") || "system";
			} catch {}
			buttons.forEach((b) =>
				b.addEventListener("click", () => {
					theme = b.dataset.themeSet ?? "system";
					try {
						localStorage.setItem("whoami-theme", theme);
					} catch {}
					apply(theme);
				}),
			);
			apply(theme);
		</script>
</Base>

<style>
	/* Demo scaffolding plus the landing and UI samples, which stay here until
	   they become real components. Prose, links, code, focus and motion all
	   come from the global layers. */
	.page {
		max-width: 64rem;
		margin-inline: auto;
		padding: 0 var(--space-3) var(--space-9);
	}

	.switcher {
		position: sticky;
		top: 0;
		z-index: 10;
		display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		gap: var(--space-2);
		align-items: center;
		background: var(--ground);
		border-block-end: 1px solid var(--rule);
		margin-inline: calc(var(--space-3) * -1);
		margin-block-end: var(--space-6);
		padding: var(--space-3);
	}

	.thm {
		font-family: var(--font-ui);
		font-variation-settings: var(--axes-ui);
		font-size: var(--text-meta);
		font-weight: 500;
		padding: var(--space-1) var(--space-2);
		border: 1px solid var(--rule-strong);
		border-radius: var(--radius);
		background: none;
		color: var(--dim);
		cursor: pointer;
	}

	.thm[aria-pressed="true"] {
		color: var(--ground);
		background: var(--accent);
		border-color: var(--accent);
	}

	.chrome-label {
		font-family: var(--font-code);
		font-variation-settings: var(--axes-code);
		font-size: var(--text-micro);
		font-weight: 500;
		letter-spacing: 0.1em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		color: var(--faint);
		margin-block-end: var(--space-2);
	}

	.switcher .chrome-label {
		margin: 0;
	}

	.page-title {
		font-size: var(--text-section);
		margin-block-end: var(--space-3);
	}

	.page-note {
		font-size: var(--text-small);
		color: var(--dim);
		max-width: var(--measure);
		margin-block-end: var(--space-7);
	}

	.frame {
		border: 1px solid var(--rule);
		border-radius: var(--radius);
		padding: var(--space-5) var(--space-4);
		margin-block-end: var(--space-7);
	}

	.frame > .chrome-label {
		margin-block-end: var(--space-5);
	}

	.code-samples {
		max-width: var(--measure);
	}

	/* ---- landing sample ---- */
	.landing-nav {
		display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		gap: var(--space-4);
		align-items: baseline;
		font-family: var(--font-ui);
		font-variation-settings: var(--axes-ui);
		font-size: var(--text-meta);
		font-weight: 500;
		margin-block-end: var(--space-8);
	}

	.landing-nav .brand {
		font-family: var(--font-heading);
		font-size: var(--text-sub);
		font-weight: 700;
		margin-inline-end: auto;
	}

	.landing-nav a {
		color: var(--dim);
		text-decoration: none;
	}

	.landing-nav a:hover {
		color: var(--ink);
	}

	.hero {
		font-family: var(--font-heading);
		font-size: var(--text-display);
		font-weight: 700;
		line-height: var(--leading-display);
		text-wrap: balance;
		margin-block-end: var(--space-5);
	}

	.hero-lead {
		font-size: var(--text-lead);
		line-height: var(--leading-lead);
		max-width: var(--measure);
		margin-block-end: var(--space-7);
	}

	.work-list {
		list-style: none;
		padding: 0;
		margin: 0;
		border-block-start: 1px solid var(--rule);
	}

	.work-item {
		display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		gap: var(--space-3);
		align-items: baseline;
		padding-block: var(--space-3);
		border-block-end: 1px solid var(--rule);
	}

	.work-item h3 {
		flex: 1 1 14rem;
	}

	.work-item p {
		flex: 2 1 18rem;
		font-size: var(--text-small);
		color: var(--dim);
	}

	.work-item .year {
		font-family: var(--font-code);
		font-variation-settings: var(--axes-code);
		font-size: var(--text-meta);
		font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
		color: var(--faint);
	}

	/* ---- interface samples ---- */
	.ui-grid {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(15rem, 1fr));
		gap: var(--space-5);
	}

	.ui-group h4 {
		font-family: var(--font-code);
		font-variation-settings: var(--axes-code);
		font-size: var(--text-micro);
		font-weight: 500;
		letter-spacing: 0.1em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		color: var(--faint);
		margin-block-end: var(--space-3);
	}

	.btn-row,
	.tag-row {
		display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		gap: var(--space-2);
		align-items: center;
	}

	.btn {
		font-family: var(--font-ui);
		font-variation-settings: var(--axes-ui);
		font-size: var(--text-meta);
		font-weight: 600;
		padding: var(--space-2) var(--space-3);
		border: 1px solid currentColor;
		border-radius: var(--radius);
		background: none;
		color: inherit;
		cursor: pointer;
	}

	.btn.solid {
		background: var(--accent);
		border-color: var(--accent);
		color: var(--ground);
	}

	.btn.quiet {
		border-color: var(--rule-strong);
		color: var(--dim);
	}

	.tag {
		font-family: var(--font-code);
		font-variation-settings: var(--axes-code);
		font-size: var(--text-micro);
		font-weight: 500;
		letter-spacing: 0.06em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		color: var(--dim);
		border: 1px solid var(--rule);
		border-radius: var(--radius);
		padding: 0.2em 0.5em;
	}

	.field {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: var(--space-1);
	}

	.field label {
		font-family: var(--font-code);
		font-variation-settings: var(--axes-code);
		font-size: var(--text-micro);
		font-weight: 500;
		letter-spacing: 0.1em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		color: var(--faint);
	}

	.field input {
		font-size: var(--text-small);
		padding: var(--space-2);
		border: 1px solid var(--rule-strong);
		border-radius: var(--radius);
		background: none;
		color: inherit;
	}

	.field .hint {
		font-size: var(--text-small);
		color: var(--dim);
	}

	.stat {
		display: block;
		font-family: var(--font-code);
		font-variation-settings: var(--axes-code);
		font-size: var(--text-section);
		font-weight: 600;
		font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
		color: var(--secondary);
	}

	.stat-label,
	.meta-sample {
		font-family: var(--font-ui);
		font-variation-settings: var(--axes-ui);
		font-size: var(--text-meta);
		color: var(--dim);
	}
</style>
